{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FhsJRraivqAwGJ6V81o1Nn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the workspace's root `CLAUDE.md`, here's what this project **is**:\n\n- **It's a personal AI-agent research sandbox** â€” John Liechty's \"Agentic Home\" / Agentic Sandbox at `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`, a workspace for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. It's explicitly a research project, not a production system, and most of its ~80 root folders are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs) rather than runnable code.\n\n- **The active shippable deliverable is a GUI app** â€” the **Ghost World Labs (GWL-M) master GUI**, a Next.js app in `sandbox-lab-gui/` (launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`) that opens a dashboard at `localhost:3001` to launch and supervise agents, with a per-agent terminal model and a Settings Vault for API keys.\n\n- **It runs agents on the OpenClaw runtime** â€” a global MIT-licensed npm package. The GUI dispatches turns through `agent-chat.mjs` â†’ `openclaw agent`, with a canonical agent registry/routing in `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`. The daily-use vehicle is `alpha-v0`, a t2r (\"taste â†’ reason\") dispatcher agent; other agents are research/legacy or planned-but-unbuilt.\n\n- **It ships a custom \"sovereign\" t2r/t2rs harness + brain architecture** â€” a cost-controlled ReAct loop (`gwl-t2r-brain/harness/`) layered over remote LLMs with caching, tier-routing, per-turn cost ledgers, and provider portability (Anthropic live; Gemini/OpenAI/Grok built). M1 is feature-complete for Google+Anthropic. The longer-term goal is to **distill frontier models into small local students** (QLoRA on â‰¤8B models on the box's RTX 4070).\n\n- **It includes a skill ecosystem and orchestration tooling** â€” a master skill repo (`skills-master/`) linked into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and OpenClaw, plus a planning/build trio (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) that drives multi-wave autonomous builds from frozen plan docs.\n\n- **Supporting infrastructure rounds it out** â€” a Settings Vault API-key contract (subscription for interactive sessions vs. metered API keys for sandbox agents), structured logging under `logs/`, nightly GitHub backups, and an extensive corpus of architecture whitepapers (memory architecture, geometric/PoincarÃ© memory, \"half a brain,\" watcher layer) and a K-12 curriculum deliverable.\n\nOne note: your message ends with \"Anchors from the project documents:\" but no anchors followed, and there's an untracked `.anchor/` directory and `Anchor.md` in the working tree. If you wanted me to ground these bullets against specific anchor excerpts (or to read `Anchor.md`), say the word and I'll pull them in."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20230,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20230},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"003b302f-720c-44ff-a35a-94a99630e787","uuid":"cbfb988e-ca72-4018-883f-e9c9b6ecc495","request_id":"req_011Cc3tgd9sVWigfaa1MumwF"}
